.TH "BURROW" "1" "Oct 2026" "burrow 0.1.0-dev" "burrow manual"

.SH NAME
burrow-purge - deprecated alias for: burrow clean --only projects


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBburrow purge [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Deprecated alias for \fBburrow clean --only projects\fR\&.

.PP
Finds rebuildable build artifacts (node_modules, target, virtualenvs,
\fBpycache\fP, ...) under the configured project roots and moves them to the
Trash. Artifacts are kept when they are git-tracked, when git state cannot be
determined, when they contain a git repository, when their activity age cannot
be verified, or when they have seen file activity within the age window.
Trashed artifacts are recoverable (burrow history --restore); nothing is
permanently deleted.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--age\fP=""
	only artifacts with no activity in this window (default 7d)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for purge

.PP
\fB--paths\fP[=false]
	print the configured project roots


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	terminal color policy: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	override the config file path

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	never mutate; print the plan and exit

.PP
\fB--exclude\fP=[]
	comma list of categories or item ids to exclude

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable output

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="info"
	trace|debug|info|warn|error

.PP
\fB--min-size\fP="0"
	only act on items >= size (e.g. 10M, 1G)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable color (same as --color=never)

.PP
\fB--no-owner\fP[=false]
	skip all owner-command/system acts

.PP
\fB--only\fP=[]
	comma list of categories or item ids to include

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	non-interactive plain-text output instead of the TUI

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	only print errors

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
